# MSX2 reference sources

Consult these as primary technical references for MSX2 hardware, BIOS, VDP, I/O, and system behavior:

- **MSX Technical Data Book** — https://download.file-hunter.com/Manuals/msx_technical_data_book.pdf
  - Local copy: `docs/references/msx-technical-data-book.md`
- **MSX2 Technical Handbook** (Konamiman, markdown) — https://github.com/Konamiman/MSX2-Technical-Handbook
  - Covers: system overview, BASIC, MSX-DOS, VDP/display, BIOS peripheral access, BIOS listing, MATH-PACK, bit-block transfer, work area, VRAM map, I/O map, cartridge hardware, control codes, character set.
- **MSX Wiki** — community reference for programming, hardware, graphics, music, and design:
  - Programming — https://www.msx.org/wiki/Category:Programming
  - Graphics — https://www.msx.org/wiki/Category:Graphics
  - Music — https://www.msx.org/wiki/Category:Music
  - Game Design — https://www.msx.org/wiki/Game_Design
  - Hardware Design — https://www.msx.org/wiki/Hardware_Design
- **MSX BIOS calls list** (Grauw) — https://map.grauw.nl/resources/msxbios.php
  - Local copy: `docs/references/msx-bios-calls.md`
- **MSX system variables** (Grauw) — https://map.grauw.nl/resources/msxsystemvars.php
  - Local copy: `docs/references/msx-system-variables.md`
- **openMSX user manual** — https://openmsx.org/manual/user.html
  - Local copy: `docs/references/openmsx-user-manual.html`

Prefer these over recalled details when they conflict; cite the specific chapter/appendix when relevant.
